+# draft-welcome-call: Create a welcome call task when a person registers
+
+- **Jira:** none yet
+- **Gate:** normal
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:**
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** journey. Touches: identity through the event `identity.person-registered` (consumed, unchanged); apps/worker registers the subscription
+
+## Context
+
+When a person registers, the advisor must call them. Journey creates a welcome call task for each new person so that it appears in the task list.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+No Discovery AC covers this rule yet. The tests have no AC ID in their titles. A person assigns the AC ID with the Jira key.
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| none | `packages/core/src/journey/journey.test.ts`, `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** journey: public API `registerJourneySubscriptions(bus, { repo, bus, clock })` and `WELCOME_CALL_KIND`; Events: consumes `identity.person-registered`; invariant: one `welcome-call` task per person.
+- **Contracts:** none new. Consumes `identity.person-registered` (`personId`, `brand`) as it is.
+- **Schema:** none. The task row uses the existing columns of `journey.task`.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- Task: kind `welcome-call`, title `Welcome call`, due date `businessDate(event.occurredAt)`. The registration time, not the handling time, so a late delivery from the queue keeps the date.
+- Idempotency: the handler skips the person when a `welcome-call` task exists. A unique index on (`person_id`, `kind`) for this kind is for the Drizzle repository.
+- The new import journey → identity is a type import of the event, through `identity/index.ts`, in the direction the event conventions give (the reacting module imports the emitting one). No cycle.
+- A fixed handler, not the configurable journey engine (A4-C-001): the engine does not exist yet.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- The journey engine, task reasons, step lists and escalation.
+- Assigning the task to a specific advisor.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Should the welcome call later become a configured journey with trigger "days after registration" (0 days)?
+- The task has no reason and no step list yet, which A4-AC-002 asks of every task. Is that acceptable until the task list story? If not, this story contradicts A4-AC-002 and becomes a design story (trigger 5).
+- Idempotency is check-then-write. The Drizzle repository needs a unique index on (`person_id`, `kind`) for `welcome-call` so that two parallel deliveries cannot both write.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
